  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>A favorite among intelligence agents, undercover law enforcement, and criminals in need of a well-concealed Weapon, the Snap-Shot Blaster Pistol is a variant of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Hold-Out_Blaster_Pistol\" title=\"Hold-Out Blaster Pistol\">Hold-Out Blaster Pistol</a> often perceived as a last resort weapon. Morrigan Corde uses a Snap-Shot Blaster Pistol in emergencies. </p><p>A Snap-Shot Blaster Pistol carries a single round of ammunition in its <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>, and because of its compact design, a Snap-Shot Blaster Pistol grants a +5 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> bonus on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a> checks made to conceal the Weapon. </p><p>A Snap-Shot Blaster Pistol requires a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;to operate. After one shot, the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;must be replaced. </p>",
